//? Title: Self-organizing maps: explicit native tensor SGD and actual neighborhood winners
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Fit a rectangular grid of prototype vectors to unlabelled inputs by moving a best-matching unit and its grid neighbors toward each sampled observation. Native tensors compute every winner, neighborhood, objective and update; the original three-blob,5-by-5,4000-update experiment retains its actual input and sampling streams.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

For one input x, the lowest-index nearest codebook unit b is the discrete best-matching unit. Freeze b while differentiating the step objective
$$ L_t(W)=\frac12\sum_k h_{bk}(t)\|w_k-x_t\|^2,\qquad h_{bk}=\exp(-\|r_b-r_k\|^2/(2\sigma_t^2)). $$
\alttext(The frozen-winner step objective is half the sum of grid-neighborhood-weighted squared codebook distances to the sampled input.)
Its codebook gradient is h_bk*(w_k-x), so plain SGD at alpha_t gives w_k+=alpha_t*h_bk*(x-w_k). Native influences below1e-6 are set to zero, matching the scalar reference. The input, winner and decaying radius change between steps; this is not descent on one fixed smooth global objective and does not guarantee topology preservation. The report explicitly creates Float64 learnable codebook leaves, selects Sgd, supplies the scheduled rate and calls minimize in the visible loop. Generating blob labels color plots only.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/self_organizing_map_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace a = dm::algorithms;
  namespace g = dm::graphics;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  auto               weights  = n::from_vector(std::vector<double>{0, 2}, {2, 1}).requires_grad_();
  auto               sample   = n::from_vector(std::vector<double>{1});
  auto               grid     = n::from_vector(std::vector<double>{0, 0, 0, 1}, {2, 2});
  auto               step     = n::som_neighborhood_objective(weights, sample, grid, 1);
  auto               gradient = n::grad(step.objective, std::vector<n::Tensor>{weights});
  n::OptimizerConfig config;
  config.kind = n::OptimizerKind::Sgd;
  n::Optimizer optimizer(std::vector<n::Tensor>{weights}, .5, config);
  std::print(
      "Actual frozen winner {}, influences `{}`, objective {}, gradient `{}`.\n",
      step.winner,
      step.influence.to_vector<double>(),
      step.objective.item(),
      gradient[0].to_vector<double>());
  optimizer.step(gradient);
  std::print(
      "Actual codebook after one explicit Sgd step at0.5: `{}`.\n", weights.to_vector<double>());
  g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
  concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Explicit codebook leaf [0,2], input1");
  concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0}, std::format("Actual tensor winner {}", step.winner));
  concept_diagram.node(
      "n2", {10, 0}, std::format("Actual SGD weights {:.3f}, {:.3f} (rounded)",weights.at({0,0}),weights.at({1,0})));
  concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
  concept_diagram.save_svg("build/self_organizing_map_tiny.svg");
}
```
